  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="c3e6-3716-82f3-5cef" name="Spanish (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #13 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). 500 BC to 72 BC The Iberians traded with the Phoenician colonies from around 1100 BC but remained independent until the coming of (briefly) the Barcas and then (more permanently) the Romans. After the defeat of Carthage, the Romans still struggled to subjugate the tribes, and revolts continued down to the Principate. The list may also be used to create a Celtiberian force from those tribes under Gallic cultural influence. Allies: No allies are available to a Spanish army.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Spanish]
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Skirmishers: up to 10%
  Characters: up to 25% Infantry: At least 50% Cavalry: Up to 25% Skirmishers: Up to 10%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
